{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is an isosceles triangle in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e90d34a78667f6d5c71cf3dde1627d01e1a52132.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = 92^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is extended to a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. What is the size of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93e72b9d2c86f197276a931aba77c472d0511c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2ef511a282eb884f91c071c3e962b079e1a552b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 88^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 44^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 92^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 136^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 158^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"490\" height=\"19\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/0/510e2cf258111f88acfbceaeced6b3485f6b6569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABC$\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />. For the triangle to be isosceles, there has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equal angles, so either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aea3184063ae2117b4d51d0f980204525ce6005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABC = m\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"169\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a24351c4001d06f7b19b7cfbd1d537b76d28f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ACB = 92^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/950f71d116fedab94dff14e7737448af830f58b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABC = 92^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>However, the last two are impossible because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/16907440ad5963e9bea6ab75d4ccd40ecc7f2e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$92^{\\circ} + 92^{\\circ} = 184^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" />, which is more than the number of degrees in a triangle. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6f41c9fc1bafd44724830585dc753860a5e4a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABC = m\\angle ACB = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"204\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Using the fact that the sum of the measurements of the angles in a triangle is always equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26af970522698617c6590ca12c0a1bf7200e6bc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 92 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60d320e11d05731db8b422afb7f990d1941c6223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 88$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdae68123ed163e176752b6ebd0baa91d2f372b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the extension of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/d/87da4992deed43fafdcdf6879ffb693fd6414995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CBD$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> must be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Straight_angle\" title=\"Straight angle\">straight angle</a>, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808e73c19a61d229add21ce003513657a0b7f45c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />. This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/67717f4aed519b58858c9229de91c473f2934c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABD + x = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35aa6d5beadc8a10c40244e0b2e459d08ab1b1ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABD + 44 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f6d19dee7ceb0108a9b3a9e1bc5cf0457a6be1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABD = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 136^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"181\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can also notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85a0bc0ee6d62f7b6a89feb56e98f81f12fbce7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ABD = 180 - (180 - 92 - x) = 92 + x = 92 + 44 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 136^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"527\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192747\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 155/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 440/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5221/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.921      1 Template:Image_needed\n100.00%    5.921      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:32512:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017192747 and revision id 251486. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}